"""Whole-exchange B157 decisions: explicit revisions and individual wording retentions."""
REVISIONS={
5:("The usual amount of cinnamon, please.","Restore that the quantity, not merely the product, is his usual order. Keep the familiar merchant's polite economy."),
13:("Sure. That'll be this much.","Make the Trader's reply an ordinary price quotation. Preserve the deictic amount without inventing a number or currency."),
24:("Ha ha, Adil. Don't be ridiculous. You think I don't know what you pay for it?","Restore his laugh and rhetorical challenge about the Trader's purchasing cost. The next turn carries the request for a better price; remove its premature duplication here."),
49:("That's not it. You've got a fever. Get to bed early tonight.","Restore the denial, fever and early-bed advice. 'You feel hot' suggested physical contact that the source does not supply; do not add an instruction to go home."),
52:("Oh, come on... Huh? I really do have the chills.","Make his shift from dismissal to recognizing his own chills sound natural. Keep it his experience, without a diagnosis or a narrator's conclusion."),
55:("See? I'll do my shopping tomorrow. Close up for today.","Restore the explicit shop closure and Carlo's deferred purchase. This explains why the waiting travelers must also return tomorrow."),
58:("All right, I'll take your advice. Sorry, folks. Please come back tomorrow.","Replace the clipped 'Travelers, sorry' with an ordinary apology. Preserve his acceptance of Carlo's advice and his request to the waiting party."),
91:("Oh? You're just as observant as I am.","Preserve Fernando's self-important comparison in natural speech. His optional boast implies no medical credentials."),
97:("... (Did he?)","Use past tense for Lil's uncertainty about the man's pallor. This row is outside Fernando's optional guard, so it must also make sense without his boast. Preserve the pause and inner question."),
101:("Most people wouldn't notice. I'm quick to notice when someone's unwell.","Give Carlo a natural explanation of his attentiveness. Preserve the contrast with most people without inventing a professional medical role."),
109:("Will you come to the trading post with me tomorrow morning? I think I can make up for today.","Restore tomorrow morning, the invitation to accompany him and the qualified offer to make up for the inconvenience. Do not turn it into cash repayment."),
112:("You're going to make it up to us, right? Then of course I'll come!","Connect Lil's eager acceptance to his promised favor. Avoid a new assertion that he owes a financial debt."),
123:("He's resting at home today, just to be safe.","Restore that resting is a precaution. Keep the woman's report separate from Adil's later self-assured claim that he is well."),
130:("He never listens to me. Yesterday, if you hadn't said something...","Restore her unfinished counterfactual about yesterday. Preserve familiar exasperation without explicitly making her Adil's wife."),
134:("Oh, listen to me rambling. You're a lifesaver! I wanted to thank you.","Restore her self-interruption and unhedged grateful praise. 'Lifesaver' remains her characterization, not proof of a fatal illness or cure."),
138:("Thank you. I appreciate it, but thank these travelers instead. They put off their business overnight.","Restore Carlo's gratitude and generous redirection. An overnight postponement is more precise than 'a day' and does not assert a timed 24-hour requirement."),
148:("Thank you, ma'am. Now, you're in a hurry, aren't you? Go ahead and do your shopping first.","Preserve his thanks to the woman and then his direct address to the travelers. Do not redirect the entire speech into a third-person order to the shopkeeper. Ma'am creates no kinship or rank."),
170:("Ha ha, I'm glad to see you so lively. Just don't overdo it today.","Keep Carlo's laugh, relief at Adil's energy and continued caution. His warmth fits the concern that the later family story explains."),
174:("I can always stop by tomorrow. Take care of these travelers' business for me.","Restore a complete, natural hand-off of trading priority and his willingness to defer his own visit. Preserve tomorrow without claiming event timing or eligibility."),
177:("Take care of your health and your families. See you around.","Keep his central advice and familiar farewell in natural American English. This prepares the theme of the later confession without stilted sermon-like wording."),
217:("Is there some reason you don't want to leave? Malacca isn't your hometown, is it?","Restore her question about an attachment to the town and the specific hometown distinction. 'Home' alone could deny his present residence; preserve the questioning tone."),
229:("First my daughter caught an illness that was going around. I was so wrapped up in my work... I didn't take proper care of her.","Keep the FE panel in Carlo's first person. Restore the circulating illness and his admission of neglect. 'Work kept me away' invented physical separation and softened his agency; add no age, pathogen or physician."),
232:("Treatment came too late, and my wife caught it too... I lost them both.","Preserve delayed treatment, spread to his wife and his personal loss of both wife and daughter. Restore first-person grief without inventing treatment procedures."),
240:("The work I'd neglected my family for felt so empty. Since then, I've cared more about people's health than business.","Restore the emptiness of what he gained by neglecting his family and the continuing change in priorities. Use natural tense and his reflective voice without adding a new medical profession."),
243:("Oh... That's why you noticed he was sick.","Lil now understands why Carlo was attentive. 'That's how' could merely repeat the earlier pallor explanation and lose the emotional cause."),
246:("Did you ever think about... going home?","Preserve her hesitant, gentle question after his loss. Avoid making the question sound like an accusation that he failed to consider an obvious remedy."),
264:("Being alone isn't much fun, is it? We'll be your family from now on.","Preserve Lil's simple, compassionate logic and explicit chosen-family promise. 'No point being alone' sounded dismissive of his grief. Invent no biological parenthood, romance or adoption procedure."),
285:("...I always say nice things. Right, Carlo?","Make her comic self-regard idiomatic while retaining the appeal to the older man. She has already heard his given name from Adil; use the known name without inventing uncle kinship."),
289:("...Thank you. Well, then... I'd like to come with you.","Give his grateful, hesitant acceptance a complete natural response. Keep the spoken invitation acceptance separate from an earned recruitment effect."),
296:("{MACRO:FI}... I have a little more respect for you now.","Restore a complete, understated sentence of new respect, rather than the fragment 'New respect.' Keep the source qualification and runtime FI substitution."),
299:("I'm Carlo Sinat. Pleased to meet you.","Restore a full introduction using the bound approved native spelling Carlo Sinat. The predecessor's Sinato conflicts with that spelling; do not introduce a guessed alternative surname.")
}
